Findings for planning the photos page revival.

## 1. Git history — the old photos page

**It existed in the Pages Router era and was removed in two steps:**

| Commit | What happened |
|---|---|
| `5feff5c` "add photos" | first photos page |
| `96da4cf` "Imporovments to typing and adds photo page. Closes #43" | V2 photos page (parallax grid + EXIF) |
| `a4b3094` "implement-back-button-photos-page" | back button added to `src/components/ui/photos.tsx` (issue #48) |
| `9582758` "hotfix" | **disabled** photos — commented out everything and renamed `src/pages/photos.tsx` → `src/pages/photos.tsx.txt` |
| `28a7875` "wip" | **deleted** everything — the Pages Router → App Router rewrite; removed all `photos` source files, the `scripts/photography_rename.sh`, `src/styles/PhotoGrid.module.css`, and all **133 JPGs** under `public/images/photography/` |

Last live (uncommented) versions are at `9582758^`. Files that existed:

- `src/pages/photos.tsx` — page (client-side fetch from `/api/photos`, then per-file `/api/photos/metadata/[filename]`)
- `src/components/ui/photos.tsx` — `ParallaxScroll` 3-column framer-motion grid with EXIF overlay on hover
- `src/components/PhotoGrid.tsx` — simpler CSS-grid variant (unused by the photos page)
- `src/styles/PhotoGrid.module.css`
- `src/pages/api/photos/index.tsx` — `fs.readdirSync("public/images/photography/")`
- `src/pages/api/photos/metadata/[filename].tsx` — `exif` package `ExifImage` read
- `src/lib/interfaces.ts` — `Photo`, `TextEntry`, `PhotoOrText` types
- `scripts/photography_rename.sh` — renames photos to `001.jpg`, `002.jpg`, …

Retrieve any of them with e.g. `git show 9582758^:src/pages/photos.tsx`. The 133 original images are recoverable: `git show '28a7875^:public/images/photography/001.jpg'` (list via `git ls-tree -r --name-only 28a7875^ -- public/images/photography`). Sizes were large — several were 3–7 MB unoptimized JPGs, which is exactly what caused the closed bugs.

### The old page component (from `9582758^:src/pages/photos.tsx`, comment markers stripped)

```tsx
export default function Photos() {
  const [photos, setPhotos] = useState<PhotoOrText[]>([]);
  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchPhotos = async () => {
      const response = await fetch("/api/photos");
      const data: string[] = await response.json();
      const photosWithMetadata = await Promise.all(
        data.map(async (file_name) => {
          const metaResponse = await fetch(`/api/photos/metadata/${file_name}`);
          const metadata = await metaResponse.json();
          return { file_name, metadata, image: `/images/photography/${file_name}` } as Photo;
        }),
      );
      setPhotos(photosWithMetadata);
    };
    fetchPhotos();
  }, []);

  const staticPhotos = useMemo(() => [
    { name: "Here's a gallery of some of my photos I've taken. You can view them all on my Instagram @jasper.mayone.photography", type: "text" } as TextEntry,
    ...photos,
  ], [photos]);

  return (
    <>
      <DotsBackground />
      <div className="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center px-5">
        <div className="w-full flex justify-center mt-5">
          <ParallaxScroll className="h-full w-full" photos={staticPhotos} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </>
  );
}
```

`ParallaxScroll` (`src/components/ui/photos.tsx`) split `photos` into thirds, applied `useScroll`/`useTransform` offsets of `-200 / +200 / -200` per column, rendered each `next/image` at 400×400 with a hover overlay listing Camera Make/Model, F-Stop, Focal Length, ISO, Shutter Speed, Aperture, Brightness, Lens, Exposure Time. The first entry was a `TextEntry` card containing the intro copy and a `← Back` link to `/`.

**Known problems with the old design (all closed issues):** #50 page took forever to load, #53 wanted pagination/infinite scroll, #51 Vercel serverless function too large, #49 EXIF broke after a move to S3, #48 no back button, #7 wanted a popover.

The home page linked to it: the word "photographer" in the intro paragraph was `<Link href="/photos">`, and "Photos" was in the header word list.

**Issue #102 ("bring back photos page")** has one comment from the owner: `https://x.com/sorenblank/status/1979079948204757089 for layout` — a layout reference for the new version.

## 2. Current page conventions

Every page is a server component under `src/app/<slug>/page.tsx` with this shape (see `/Users/jsp/dev/projects/website/.claude/worktrees/rippling-skipping-muffin/src/app/conferences/page.tsx` and `.../src/app/pfp/page.tsx`, the two best templates):

1. `export const metadata: Metadata` with `title`, `description`, `alternates.canonical: "https://jaspermayone.com/<slug>"`.
2. A module-level `const <name>PageSchema` JSON-LD `@graph` containing a `WebPage` node (with `isPartOf` → `#website`, `about` → `#person`, `mainEntity`, and a `BreadcrumbList` Home → Page) plus a domain node. **`pfp/page.tsx` already uses `"@type": "ImageGallery"` with `ImageObject` entries — directly reusable for photos.**
3. Rendered via `<Script id="<slug>-schema" type="application/ld+json" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: safeJsonLd(schema) }} />` (`src/lib/jsonld.ts`).
4. Body: `<div className="flex min-h-screen flex-col"><MENU pageFirstWord="..." /><main className="flex-1"><div className="mx-5 mt-4 mb-4"> … </div></main><FOOTER /></div>`
5. Headings use `style={{ fontFamily: "var(--font-balgin)" }}`; text colors `text-zinc-800 dark:text-white` / `text-zinc-600 dark:text-white/70`.

`MENU` (`src/components/MENU.tsx`) composes `AnimatedTitle` + `PageNavigation` + `SquigglyLine` — you never use those three directly. Props: `pageFirstWord`, `pageSecondWord?`, `pageThirdWord?`, `color?`, `disableSquig?`, `addBackground?`.

View transitions: `next-view-transitions`. `ViewTransitions` wraps children in `src/app/layout.tsx:453`; pages import `{ Link } from "next-view-transitions"` (not `next/link`) for internal links; `PageNavigation` uses `useTransitionRouter`. `RoundedImage` accepts a `transitionName` prop that sets `viewTransitionName` — useful for a grid→detail photo transition.

## 3. Image handling

- `next.config.ts` `images:` block only has `remotePatterns` for `jasper.cv` and `minimumCacheTTL: 60`. **No `formats`, `deviceSizes`, or remote CDN configured** — a remote photo host (S3/Immich/Cloudflare) would need a new `remotePatterns` entry, and the CSP `img-src 'self' data: https: blob:` already allows any https origin.
- Static imports are the norm: `import jm from "@public/images/profiles/jm.webp"` (`@public/*` alias in `tsconfig.json`), which enables `placeholder="blur"` automatically. `pfp/page.tsx` does exactly this.
- `public/images/` currently holds: `confetti/`, `logos/`, `panera/`, `profiles/`, `projects/`, plus `CROP.jpg`, `jmdark-min.webp`, `jmlite-min.webp`. **No `photography/` directory exists anymore.** Assets are `.webp` now, not `.jpg`.
- `src/components/RoundedImage.tsx` is the only image wrapper component.
- No `sharp`/`exif` dependency in `package.json` today — EXIF extraction would have to be reintroduced (better at build time / as static data than at request time, given issue #51).

## 4. `defs.ts` / `types.ts` — no photos entry currently

- `src/lib/defs.ts:63` `export const pages: PageItem[]` — **no photos entry.** Add `{ text: "Photos", slug: "photos", showInNav: false, order: 99 }` (or `showInNav: true` with a low order). `PageItem` is `{ text, slug, showInNav, order }` in `src/lib/types.ts:9`.
- `src/lib/defs.ts:1069` `export const slashPages: SlashPage[]` — no photos entry; add `{ slug: "photos", name: "Photos", description: "…" }` so it shows on `/slashes`.
- The only current "photo" hits in `defs.ts` are `src/lib/defs.ts:849` (`{ emoji: "📷", name: "Photos", result: "iOS Camera, Immich" }` in the /uses list — note he self-hosts **Immich**, a plausible backing source) and the Instagram link at `src/lib/defs.ts:245` (`https://www.instagram.com/jasper.mayone`).
- `src/lib/og-utils.ts` `getPageOGData` has a `pathMappings` record — add a `/photos` entry there for a custom OG image, otherwise it falls back to a title-cased slug.
- Sitemap is generated post-build by `next-sitemap` (`next-sitemap.config.js`) from the App Router routes, so a new `src/app/photos/page.tsx` is picked up automatically; only add to `highPriority`/`mediumPriority` arrays if desired.
- `src/lib/types.ts` has no `Photo` type today — the old one lived in the deleted `src/lib/interfaces.ts`; a new `Photo` interface belongs in `types.ts` alongside `Conference`/`Hackathon`.

